The METADATA section currently omits most changes ('+16 more metadata changes omitted') and renders long values inline mid-sentence. Show all main metadata info. For values like map UID and author login (and other long identifiers), format each as old and new on separate lines aligned on the left, in a monospace font, e.g.:\n\n  - Map UID: u5byRl2QnqZ6a1e_YumY._6plk\n  + Map UID: 36ROAOA.O5tyi7744S_L9xyQ1k\n\nso old/new can be compared visually. Same alignment pattern for author login, author name, map name, and any other long string values.

Lane plan: serial infographic lane B072 -> B071 -> B067 -> B073 (all touch DiffInfographic/Painter/Fonts), one worktree. B072 first: lands the DiffInfographicFonts.Mono family B071's alignment needs.

Decision (2026-09-11): two-sided metadata renders as a regular-font '~ Label' line followed by mono '- old' / '+ new' value lines (one-sided entries stay single-line mono); metadata truncation dropped entirely and DiffInfographic.MaximumHeight (2200) removed so the page grows — the SB2 v205-vs-v206 render is 1400x24084 with one very tall metadata column, which the no-required-aspect-ratio decision accepts.